{"type":"text","timestamp":1794251941733,"sessionID":"ses_e3e440ebdffe3zs16pPnbKPW5e","part":{"id":"prt_1c1bfe74b0012Vo9fUGTC4nliO","messageID":"msg_1c1bfcea0001Mu475SyhysfmQ8","sessionID":"ses_e3e440ebdffe3zs16pPnbKPW5e","type":"text","text":"The shop is built: Flask API in `backend/app.py` and a React/Tailwind frontend in `frontend/`. The backend serves the frontend build. I couldn't run Docker here, so the `Dockerfile` build is untested.\n\nWhat I did check:\n- **API:** I exercised it through Flask's test client. Registration, login and admin login work, as do paging, cart add and update, and price changes flowing into the cart. A deactivated product disappeared from the cart and from `/api/products/{id}`, and another user's cart item returned 404.\n- **Frontend:** `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` pass. I haven't loaded the UI in a browser, so the layout and interactions are unchecked.\n\nA few behaviours you might not assume:\n- **Stock limits:** adding or setting a quantity above the available stock is rejected with 409 and a message such as \"Only 40 in stock\". Adding to the cart still doesn't change stock.\n- **Add status codes:** `POST /api/cart` answers 201 both for a new item and when it increases an existing one.\n- **Admin:** `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is read at start. If it's unset or empty, admin login is refused and any existing admin session stops working.\n- **Extra endpoints:** I added `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/admin/products`. The last one lists inactive products too, so the admin screen can re-activate them.\n- **Seed data:** the first start loads 10 products, each with stock of at least 12.\n\nI added `tailwindcss`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `typescript` and the React type packages to `frontend/package.json`, so `package-lock.json` changed too. I also added a `.gitignore` and a `typecheck` script.","time":{"start":1794251941707,"end":1794251941712}}}
